0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the 6502 (NMOS opcodes only)
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-24). -n? does no more editing than
0000                             ;        Backspace. Ctrl-C stops every build (see the console layer); the
0000                             ;        break-off cell is BRKOFF, $047B.
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter; see b8s-z80.asm for the common ideas.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  This interpreter keeps the data stack in pages 2 and 3 (252 cells) and
0000                             ;  uses 10 bytes of zero page ($00-$09). b8s-6502-zp.asm is a smaller interpreter that
0000                             ;  keeps the stack in zero page instead (112 cells); its memory map and
0000                             ;  machine-code contract differ.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks: whatever the spec calls unsafe is not caught
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build, as in the spec's "Errors and checked
0000                             ;                 builds": at startup every word cell points at 0000h (see
0000                             ;                 e_undef) and the variables and the interpreter's cells are
0000                             ;                 0. It stops with S s R r (stack over/underflow), H (heap),
0000                             ;                 O (a store outside the program's space), U (undefined
0000                             ;                 word), Q (no closing quote), W (bad character after [), X
0000                             ;                 (a reserved byte), Z (divide by zero), N (brackets) or B
0000                             ;                 (Ctrl-C), printing the spec's four-line report:
0000                             ;                   Err Z @ 3,4
0000                             ;                   0/ "no"$
0000                             ;                   Stk 2: 5 0
0000                             ;                   Rtn 0
0000                             ;                 and then goes to EXIT.
0000                             ;    ANSI     what the console escapes of "$" (/00bbIC8= /| /` /~) do:
0000                             ;             1 = send ANSI (VT100) sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = call the machine's own routines CONCLS, CONEOL, CONCUR and
0000                             ;                 CONAT (see the equates)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, C6502 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console escapes send ANSI sequences
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Registers and zero page
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    IP      zero-page pointer to the next program character (16 bits)
0000                             ;    TL/TH   the top data-stack cell (TOS) lives in zero page, not in memory
0000                             ;    X       data-stack index. The stack is two byte-planes, grows down, and
0000                             ;            holds everything under TOS: NOS is DSL,X (low) and DSH,X (high).
0000                             ;            The stack never leaves its planes because X is 8 bits.
0000                             ;    S       the hardware stack is the RETURN stack: a word call or "(" pushes
0000                             ;            the reading position (high byte first, then low) and "]" or ")"
0000                             ;            pulls it. 100 entries (200 bytes) fit with room to spare.
0000                             ;    Y, A    scratch. Y is 0 after peek/getc, and the zero-page indirect reads
0000                             ;            (IP),Y rely on that.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch: step is called with JSR, so a handler ends with a plain RTS and
0000                             ;  lands on "JMP next" in the loop. Punctuation goes through PTAB with the
0000                             ;  RTS trick (push handler-1, RTS). Handlers that use the return stack ( ( ) \
0000                             ;  ] 00bbIA== and word calls ) first pull the 2-byte JSR frame off (PLA PLA) and end
0000                             ;  with JMP next instead.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Every punctuation handler starts with the carry clear (the range sort in
0000                             ;  step leaves it so). Several of them count on that, where the comments say.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Machine-code contract (the grave): the code at TOS is entered as a
0000                             ;  subroutine, by JMP (T0) with the loop's return address on the hardware
0000                             ;  stack, so it ends with RTS (60h, which the hex loader appends). On entry
0000                             ;  TL/TH ($02/$03) hold the new TOS (the address is already consumed) and X is
0000                             ;  the data-stack index: NOS is DSL,X (low) and DSH,X (high), which is
0000                             ;  $0200,X and $0300,X.
0000                             ;  To push: DEX, store TL/TH at DSL,X/DSH,X, then set TL/TH. To drop: load
0000                             ;  TL/TH from DSL,X/DSH,X and INX. The code may change A, Y, X (it is the
0000                             ;  stack index, so it must stay consistent on return) and zero page $04-$06
0000                             ;  and $08-$09; it must keep IP ($00/$01) and the hardware stack balanced. On
0000                             ;  return TL/TH are the TOS. Zero page $0A-$0F is free for the code's own use.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                IP:       EQU   00h   ; 00-01 reading position
0000                TL:       EQU   02h   ; TOS low
0000                TH:       EQU   03h   ; TOS high
0000                T0:       EQU   04h   ; scratch
0000                T1:       EQU   05h   
0000                T2:       EQU   06h   
0000                D0:       EQU   08h   ; divisor (division, number printing)
0000                D1:       EQU   09h   
0000                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   07h   ; a key held back by the break check (0: none)
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CHECKED   
                    PLACE:    EQU   06h   ; 06-07 (T2 and $07) the address of the
                                 ;   character being run, for the error report:
                                 ;   no handler of the checked build uses T2.
                                 ;   (Machine code may change T2: that matters
                                 ;   only if it also leaves a stack overrun,
                                 ;   whose report then shows a wrong place.)
                    RSV:      EQU   LET+35h   ; S as it was before this character
                    KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; a key held back by the break check (0: none)
                                 ; The error report runs after the program, so it may use the zero page that
                                 ; machine code has ($0A-$0F):
                    CL:       EQU   0Ah   ; 0A-0B the column being reported
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    0000-00FF  zero page: the variables above
0000                             ;    0100-01FF  hardware stack = return stack, S starts at FF
0000                             ;    0200       DSL, data stack, low bytes (X = FC when empty: 252 cells)
0000                             ;    0300       DSH, data stack, high bytes
0000                             ;    0400       LET  letter cells: A..Z at +00..+33, a..z at +40..+73 (a word
0000                             ;               cell is 64 bytes below its variable), heap pointer at +7C,
0000                             ;               the -n? line buffer at +80..+FF. The checked build's cells
0000                             ;               are in the gaps: RSV at +35, PEND at +38, KEYBUF (the held
0000                             ;               key; $07 in the unchecked build) at +7A; and every build's:
0000                             ;               CDOWN at +79, BRKOFF (the break-off cell) at +7B.
0000                             ;    0500       PROG the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap follows
0000                             ;    E000       the interpreter (ROM)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the page range LETPAGE..HEAPLIM-1.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (it does
0000                             ;   if the routine ends with LDA / RTS).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve X and Y.
0000                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the console escapes of "$" call these. All four must keep X;
                                 ; they may change A, Y and the flags.
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Ch   ; /{  clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; /}  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF12h   ; /| and /`  show the cursor if the carry is set,
                                 ;     hide it if the carry is clear
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF15h   ; /~  the cursor to row A, column Y, both
                                 ;     counted from 0
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                DSL:      EQU   0200h   ; data stack, low bytes
0000                DSH:      EQU   0300h   ; data stack, high bytes
0000                DSE:      EQU   0FCh   ; X when the data stack is empty
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   04h   
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                PROG:     EQU   0500h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                PROG1:    EQU   PROG+1   
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0E0h   ; the heap must stay below E000h (a page)
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer (the heap top)
0000                CDOWN:    EQU   LET+79h   ; the break check's countdown (see pnext)
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ; the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                PEND:     EQU   LET+38h   ; checked: the program's end, where the heap
0000                             ;   starts: it may not be released below it
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   20h   ; lowest S allowed (checked build)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ;   (each pass calls KEY once; the wait for a
0000                             ;   second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms)
0000                CWAIT:    EQU   250*MSLOOP/256   ; (that wait, in 256s)
E000                          .ORG   0E000h   
E000                             ; =============================================================================
E000                             ;  Startup: find the NUL, the heap starts after it
E000                             ; =============================================================================
E000   A2 FF        START:    LDX   #0FFh   
E002   9A                     TXS      ; return stack empty
E003                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; The first half of the letter page is zeroed: every variable, every
                                 ; cell of the interpreter's own (no key held back), and every word
                                 ; cell, which then points at 0000h: calling an undefined word stops
                                 ; with U (see e_undef).
                              INX      
                              TXA      ; A = 0
                              LDY   #7Fh   
                    STZ:      STA   LET,Y   
                              DEY      
                              BPL   stz   
E003                          ENDIF      
E003   20 EA E2               JSR   rstip   
E006   20 DE E2     ST1:      JSR   getc   
E009   D0 FB                  BNE   st1   ; IP ends just past the NUL
E00B                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E00B   85 07                  STA   KEYBUF   ; (A = 0) no key held, the break key on
E00D   8D 7B 04               STA   BRKOFF   
E010                          ENDIF      
E010   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E012   8D 7C 04               STA   HEAP   
E015                          IF   CHECKED   
                              STA   PEND   
E015                          ENDIF      
E015   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E017   8D 7D 04               STA   HEAP+1   
E01A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              STA   PEND+1   
E01A                          ENDIF      
E01A   20 EA E2               JSR   rstip   
E01D   A2 FC                  LDX   #DSE   
E01F                             ; =============================================================================
E01F                             ;  The inner loop
E01F                             ; =============================================================================
E01F                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
E01F                             ;  The break key. A running program reads the keyboard only through getk
E01F                             ;  (for "?") and pnext (the break check), which between them give the break
E01F                             ;  key its rules:
E01F                             ;    - Ctrl-C (03h) stops the program: silently to EXIT in the unchecked
E01F                             ;      build, with the report (B) in the checked one;
E01F                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
E01F                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
E01F                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
E01F                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
E01F                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
E01F                             ;  KEY is the host's: a waiting key in A, or A = 0 with the zero flag set.
E01F                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
E01F                             ; pnext: the break check, then (falling through) next. A word call, a true
E01F                             ; "(" and a true ")" end here, but the keyboard is looked at only once in 256
E01F                             ; of them: CDOWN counts them down. A key found is held; a Ctrl-C goes on to ctlc. (Startup
E01F                             ; falls in here too, which does no harm.)
E01F   CE 79 04     PNEXT:    DEC   CDOWN   
E022   D0 0A                  BNE   next   
E024   20 06 FF               JSR   KEY   
E027   F0 05                  BEQ   next   ; no key
E029   85 07                  STA   KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
E02B   20 87 E0               JSR   chk3   ; (Ctrl-C: back only if the break key is off)
E02E                NEXT:        
E02E                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; Both stacks are checked once per character, after it has run. The
                                 ; return stack has overrun when S is below RSLIM: an overflow leaves
                                 ; it at 1Eh or 1Fh, an underflow wraps it to 01h (no handler pulls
                                 ; more than one entry). The data stack has when X is above DSE: an
                                 ; underflow moves X up to FDh or FEh (no handler moves X by more
                                 ; than 2, but "$", whose /~ escapes each look first), and an
                                 ; overflow wraps it from 00h to FFh.
                                 ; S is kept in RSV, for the report's Rtn line (an error found inside
                                 ; a handler has its own calls on the hardware stack), and the place
                                 ; of the character about to run in PLACE.
                              TXA      ; TSX trashes X: keep it in A
                              TSX      
                              STX   RSV   
                              CPX   #RSLIM   
                              TAX      ; TAX leaves the carry alone
                              BCC   e_rstack   
                              CPX   #DSE+1   
                              BCS   e_stack   
                              LDA   IP   
                              STA   PLACE   
                              LDA   IP+1   
                              STA   PLACE+1   
E02E                          ENDIF      
E02E   20 AD E0               JSR   step   
E031   4C 2E E0               JMP   next   
E034                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; S/R are overflows, s/r underflows. After an underflow that stack counts as
                                 ; empty.
                    E_RSTACK:   LDA   RSV   
                              CMP   #10h   
                              LDA   #"R"   
                              BCS   ejmp   ; S is 1Eh-1Fh: an overflow
                              LDA   #0FFh   
                              STA   RSV   ; S wrapped to 01h: Rtn 0
                              LDA   #"r"   
                              BNE   ejmp   ; always
                    E_STACK:   CPX   #0FFh   
                              LDA   #"S"   
                              BCS   ejmp   ; X wrapped from 00h to FFh: an overflow
                              LDX   #DSE   ; an underflow: Stk 0
                              LDA   #"s"   
                    EJMP:     JMP   error   
E034                          ENDIF      
E034                             ; The handlers that work on the return stack sit here, where short branches
E034                             ; reach next and pnext.
E034                             ; "{" TOS to the return stack, "}" return stack to TOS
E034   68           H_TOR:    PLA      
E035   68                     PLA      
E036   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E038   48                     PHA      
E039   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E03B   48                     PHA      
E03C   20 0B E3               JSR   drop   
E03F   D0 ED                  BNE   next   ; always
E041   68           H_FROMR:   PLA      
E042   68                     PLA      
E043   20 0B E1               JSR   push   
E046   68                     PLA      
E047   85 02                  STA   TL   
E049   68                     PLA      
E04A   85 03                  STA   TH   
E04C   90 E0                  BCC   next   ; always: the carry is clear on the way in
E04E                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
E04E                             ; drops it and carries on. It shares "]"s code: with the carry clear, as
E04E                             ; it is here, the address popped is pushed back.
E04E   20 F3 E2     H_CLOSE:   JSR   flag   
E051   F0 1E                  BEQ   rdrop   
E053   24                     DB   24h   ; (BIT zp: steps over the SEC)
E054                             ; "]" returns: pull an address and jump to it.
E054   38           H_RET:    SEC      
E055   68                     PLA      
E056   68                     PLA      ; drop the step frame
E057   68                     PLA      
E058   85 00                  STA   IP   
E05A   68                     PLA      
E05B   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E05D   B0 CF                  BCS   next   
E05F   48                     PHA      ; ")": keep the block start
E060   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E062   48                     PHA      
E063   90 BA                  BCC   pnext   ; always: a loop-back, with the break check
E065                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
E065                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns.
E065   20 F3 E2     H_BREAK:   JSR   flag   
E068   F0 21                  BEQ   gk9   ; (an RTS)
E06A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDA   #0   ; \ takes either closer
E06A                          ENDIF      
E06A   20 52 E1               JSR   skip   
E06D   C9 29                  CMP   #")"   
E06F   D0 E3                  BNE   h_ret   
E071   68           RDROP:    PLA      
E072   68                     PLA      
E073   68                     PLA      
E074   68                     PLA      ; (the block start's high byte: never 0)
E075   D0 B7                  BNE   next   ; always
E077                             ; getk: a key for "?" in A (zero flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag
E077                             ; set when there is none. Keeps X and Y. The held key goes first, and is
E077                             ; taken out of KEYBUF.
E077   A5 07        GETK:     LDA   KEYBUF   
E079   F0 07                  BEQ   gk1   
E07B   48                     PHA      
E07C   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E07E   85 07                  STA   KEYBUF   
E080   68                     PLA      
E081   60                     RTS      
E082   20 06 FF     GK1:      JSR   KEY   
E085   F0 04                  BEQ   gk9   
E087                             ; chk3: a key in A (not 0). A Ctrl-C goes on to ctlc, which gives the 03h
E087                             ; back if it comes back at all.
E087   C9 03        CHK3:     CMP   #3   
E089   F0 01                  BEQ   ctlc   
E08B   60           GK9:      RTS      
E08C                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
E08C                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms (about 250 times MSLOOP
E08C                             ; looks: D0 counts the 256s, D1 runs on from whatever it holds) for one more
E08C                             ; key: a second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest
E08C                             ; wins). Returns A = 03h with the zero flag clear. Keeps X and Y.
E08C   AD 7B 04     CTLC:     LDA   BRKOFF   
E08F   F0 57                  BEQ   cbreak   
E091   A9 28                  LDA   #CWAIT+1   
E093   85 08                  STA   D0   
E095   20 06 FF     CT2:      JSR   KEY   
E098   D0 0A                  BNE   ct3   
E09A   C6 09                  DEC   D1   
E09C   D0 F7                  BNE   ct2   
E09E   C6 08                  DEC   D0   
E0A0   D0 F3                  BNE   ct2   
E0A2   F0 06                  BEQ   ct9   ; always: none came
E0A4   C9 03        CT3:      CMP   #3   
E0A6   F0 40                  BEQ   cbreak   
E0A8   85 07                  STA   KEYBUF   
E0AA   A9 03        CT9:      LDA   #3   
E0AC   60                     RTS      
E0AD                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E0AD                CBREAK:   EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
E0AD                          ENDIF      
E0AD                          IF   CHECKED   
                    CBREAK:   EQU   e_break   ; the checked build reports B
E0AD                          ENDIF      
E0AD                          IF   CHECKED   
                    E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C (the stacks as they stand)
                              DB   2Ch   
                    E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte, 80h-FFh
                    EJMP3:    JMP   error   
E0AD                          ENDIF      
E0AD                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; e_undef: the word cells of undefined words hold 0000h. A call there reads
                                 ; the byte at 0000h, which is IP's own low byte: 00h while IP is 0000h, so
                                 ; the call reads a NUL with IP in page zero, where no program can be. The
                                 ; call is undone first: the step frame and the return address come off the
                                 ; hardware stack, and the place is the call letter (the return address - 1).
                    E_UNDEF:   PLA      
                              PLA      ; the step frame
                              PLA      
                              SEC      
                              SBC   #1   
                              STA   PLACE   
                              PLA      
                              SBC   #0   
                              STA   PLACE+1   
                              INC   RSV   
                              INC   RSV   ; Rtn does not count the call
                              LDA   #"U"   
                              BNE   ejmp3   ; always
E0AD                          ENDIF      
E0AD                             ; step: read one character and sort it by range.
E0AD                             ;    00h          end of program
E0AD                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored
E0AD                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
E0AD                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
E0AD                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
E0AD                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
E0AD                             ; Every way out of the sort has the carry clear, except "ignored". A checked
E0AD                             ; build stops on 80h-FFh (X) and still ignores DEL.
E0AD   20 DE E2     STEP:     JSR   getc   ; flags follow A
E0B0   F0 36                  BEQ   endprog   
E0B2   38                     SEC      
E0B3   E9 21                  SBC   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
E0B5   90 30                  BCC   ign   ; 01h-20h
E0B7   C9 0F                  CMP   #0Fh   
E0B9   90 22                  BCC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: index 0-14
E0BB   E9 0F                  SBC   #0Fh   ; (carry set) A = c - 30h
E0BD   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E0BF   90 2F                  BCC   digit   
E0C1   C9 11                  CMP   #11h   
E0C3   90 16                  BCC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
E0C5   E9 11                  SBC   #11h   ; (carry set) A = c - 41h
E0C7   C9 1A                  CMP   #1Ah   
E0C9   90 20                  BCC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah
E0CB   C9 20                  CMP   #20h   
E0CD   90 0A                  BCC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
E0CF   C9 3A                  CMP   #3Ah   
E0D1   90 25                  BCC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h
E0D3   C9 3E                  CMP   #3Eh   
E0D5                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E0D5   B0 10                  BCS   ign   ; 7Fh-FFh
E0D7                          ENDIF      
E0D7                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   ign   ; 7Fh
                              BCS   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
E0D7                          ENDIF      
E0D7                             ; The three adjustments below chain. Each ADC adds the carry the one
E0D7                             ; before it left, which the constants allow for.
E0D7   E9 1A                  SBC   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: (carry clear: -1Bh) index 28-31
E0D9   69 F6        P5B:      ADC   #0F6h   ; 5Bh-60h: -10 (-9 when chained), index 22-27
E0DB   69 05        P3A:      ADC   #5   ; 3Ah-40h: +5 (+6 when chained), index 15-21
E0DD   0A           PUNCT:    ASL      ; (the index is small: the carry stays clear)
E0DE   A8                     TAY      
E0DF   B9 54 E2               LDA   PTAB+1,Y   
E0E2   48                     PHA      
E0E3   B9 53 E2               LDA   PTAB,Y   
E0E6   48                     PHA      
E0E7   60           IGN:      RTS      ; RTS trick: goes to the handler. Reached
E0E8                             ; directly, it just ends an ignored character.
E0E8                ENDPROG:      
E0E8                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDA   IP+1   ; IP in page zero: an undefined word
                              BEQ   e_undef   
E0E8                          ENDIF      
E0E8   4C 09 FF               JMP   EXIT   
E0EB                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
E0EB                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
E0EB   0A           UPPER:    ASL      
E0EC   A8                     TAY      
E0ED   38                     SEC      
E0EE   B0 2C                  BCS   pushn   ; always
E0F0                             ; Digits: the first one is in A; read the rest of the number.
E0F0   A0 00        DIGIT:    LDY   #0   
E0F2   20 01 E1               JSR   pushay   
E0F5   4C B8 E2               JMP   rdnum   
E0F8                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
E0F8   0A           LOWER:    ASL      
E0F9   A0 04                  LDY   #>LET   
E0FB   D0 04                  BNE   pushay   ; always
E0FD   A5 00        PUSHIP:   LDA   IP   ; push the reading position
E0FF   A4 01                  LDY   IP+1   
E101                             ; pushay: push a cell: A = its low byte, Y = its high byte
E101   48           PUSHAY:   PHA      
E102   20 0B E1               JSR   push   
E105   68                     PLA      
E106   85 02                  STA   TL   
E108   84 03                  STY   TH   
E10A   60                     RTS      
E10B   CA           PUSH:     DEX      ; ":" and every push (keeps Y)
E10C   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E10E   9D 00 02               STA   DSL,X   
E111   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E113   9D 00 03               STA   DSH,X   
E116   60                     RTS      
E117                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
E117                             ; the matching ")".
E117   20 F3 E2     H_OPEN:   JSR   flag   ; (keeps the carry clear)
E11A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E11A   F0 36                  BEQ   skip   
E11C                          ENDIF      
E11C                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   skpar   
E11C                          ENDIF      
E11C                             ; pushn: take the step frame off, push the reading position on the return
E11C                             ; stack, and go on. With the carry set (a word call) the reading position
E11C                             ; then becomes the address in the letter cell at LET,Y.
E11C   68           PUSHN:    PLA      
E11D   68                     PLA      ; drop the step frame
E11E   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E120   48                     PHA      
E121   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E123   48                     PHA      
E124   90 0A                  BCC   nxt   
E126   B9 00 04               LDA   LET,Y   
E129   85 00                  STA   IP   
E12B   B9 01 04               LDA   LET+1,Y   
E12E   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E130   4C 1F E0     NXT:      JMP   pnext   
E133                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
E133                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
E133                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
E133                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
E133                             ; checked build stops on it.)
E133                          IF   CHECKED   
                    DEF1:     CPY   #" "-"A"+256   
                              BEQ   def2   
                                 ; W: anything but a letter or a space after [. The place is that character,
                                 ; one past the [.
                              INC   PLACE   
                              BNE   eb1   
                              INC   PLACE+1   
                    EB1:      LDA   #"W"   
                              BNE   ejmp2   ; always
                                 ; A false ( skips: the wrong closer for it is ].
                    SKPAR:    LDA   #"]"   
                              BNE   skip   ; always
E133                          ENDIF      
E133   20 DE E2     H_DEF:    JSR   getc   
E136   38                     SEC      
E137   E9 41                  SBC   #"A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
E139   A8                     TAY      ;   lands 64 bytes up
E13A   29 DF                  AND   #0DFh   ; fold case: 0-25 only for a letter
E13C   C9 1A                  CMP   #26   
E13E                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E13E   B0 0F                  BCS   def2   ; not a letter
E140                          ENDIF      
E140                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BCS   def1   
E140                          ENDIF      
E140   98                     TYA      
E141   0A                     ASL      
E142   A8                     TAY      ; Y -> the cell
E143   A5 00                  LDA   IP   
E145   99 00 04               STA   LET,Y   
E148   A5 01                  LDA   IP+1   
E14A   99 01 04               STA   LET+1,Y   
E14D   D0 03                  BNE   skdef   ; always: no program is in page zero
E14F   20 FD E0     DEF2:     JSR   puship   ; an anonymous block: push its address
E152                SKDEF:       
E152                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDA   #")"   ; the wrong closer for [
E152                          ENDIF      
E152                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return it in A.
E152                             ; Brackets of both kinds count together; strings are stepped over whole. A
E152                             ; NUL first ends the program.
E152                             ; In the checked build A holds, on the way in, the wrong closer for the
E152                             ; opener that started the skip, kept in T0: ] for (, ) for [, and 0 for \,
E152                             ; which takes either. Meeting the wrong closer at this level, or the end
E152                             ; (a NUL, or a string that runs into it), stops with N, except for \,
E152                             ; which then ends the program as before.
E152                SKIP:        
E152                          IF   CHECKED   
                              STA   T0   
E152                          ENDIF      
E152   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E154   85 09                  STA   D1   ; depth
E156   20 DE E2     SK1:      JSR   getc   
E159                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E159   F0 8D                  BEQ   endprog   
E15B                          ENDIF      
E15B                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   sknul   
E15B                          ENDIF      
E15B   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E15D   D0 03                  BNE   sk2   
E15F   20 7E E1               JSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h (11h when checked), which
E162                             ;   matches nothing below
E162                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   sknul   ; the string ran into the end
E162                          ENDIF      
E162   C9 28        SK2:      CMP   #"("   
E164   F0 11                  BEQ   sk3   
E166   C9 5B                  CMP   #"["   
E168   F0 0D                  BEQ   sk3   
E16A   C9 29                  CMP   #")"   
E16C   F0 04                  BEQ   sk4   
E16E   C9 5D                  CMP   #"]"   
E170   D0 E4                  BNE   sk1   
E172   C6 09        SK4:      DEC   D1   
E174   10 E0                  BPL   sk1   
E176                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CMP   T0   
                              BEQ   e_nest   ; the wrong kind
E176                          ENDIF      
E176   60                     RTS      ; the closer at this level
E177   E6 09        SK3:      INC   D1   
E179   D0 DB                  BNE   sk1   
E17B                          IF   CHECKED   
                    SKNUL:    LDA   T0   
                              BNE   e_nest   ; ( and [ stop with N
                              JMP   EXIT   ; \ ends the program
                                 ; The end of "$" (h_print): the string's address goes back into TOS; then a
                                 ; closing quote drops it, and a NUL (the carry clear) is Q.
                    PQ:       PLA      
                              STA   TL   
                              PLA      
                              STA   TH   
                              BCS   pdrop   
                    E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; a string runs into the end
                              DB   2Ch   ; (BIT abs: hides the next instruction)
                    E_NEST:   LDA   #"N"   ; a skip from ( or [ found the wrong closer
                    EJMP2:    JMP   error   ;   or the end: the place is the opener
E17B                          ENDIF      
E17B                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
E17B   20 FD E0     H_STR:    JSR   puship   
E17E                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JSR   skipstr   
                              BEQ   e_quote   ; it ran into the end: the place is the 22h
                              RTS      
E17E                          ENDIF      
E17E                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
E17E                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it.
E17E                             ; Unchecked, it returns with Z set and A = 22h, and it does not look for the
E17E                             ; end. Checked, it returns with Z clear and A = 11h, or with Z set if the
E17E                             ; text ended first (a NUL, also one just after "/").
E17E                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E17E   20 DE E2     SKIPSTR:   JSR   getc   
E181   C9 2F                  CMP   #"/"   
E183   F0 05                  BEQ   ss0   
E185   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E187   D0 F5                  BNE   skipstr   
E189   60                     RTS      
E18A   20 E1 E2     SS0:      JSR   incip   
E18D   D0 EF                  BNE   skipstr   ; A is "/" here
E18F                          ENDIF      
E18F                          IF   CHECKED   
                    SKIPSTR:   JSR   getc   
                              BEQ   ss9   ; the end
                              CMP   #"/"   
                              BNE   ss1   
                              JSR   getc   ; the escaped character
                              BNE   skipstr   
                    SS9:      RTS      ; the end, just after "/"
                    SS1:      CMP   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              LSR      ; A = 11h, Z clear
                              RTS      
E18F                          ENDIF      
E18F                             ; =============================================================================
E18F                             ;  Console
E18F                             ; =============================================================================
E18F                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character from
E18F                             ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; "/" plus any other character
E18F                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /? is DEL"s "?"; "/" and """ have
E18F                             ; no bit 6, so // and /" give themselves). TOS walks along the string; the
E18F                             ; checked build keeps the address on the hardware stack meanwhile, for a Q
E18F                             ; report (see pq).
E18F                          IF   CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   LDA   TH   
                              PHA      
                              LDA   TL   
                              PHA      
                              BCC   pr0   ; always: the carry is clear on the way in
E18F                          ENDIF      
E18F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E18F                H_PRINT:   EQU   pr0   
E18F                          ENDIF      
E18F   20 17 E2     PESC0:    JSR   pesc   ; (an escape, and back into the loop)
E192   20 B8 E1     PR0:      JSR   tosget   
E195   C9 22                  CMP   #22h   
E197                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E197   F0 1C                  BEQ   pdrop   
E199                          ENDIF      
E199                          IF   CHECKED   
                              BEQ   pq   ; the closing quote, with the carry set
                              TAY      ; (Y is free here)
                              BEQ   pq   ; a NUL, with the carry clear
E199                          ENDIF      
E199   C9 2F                  CMP   #"/"   
E19B   D0 0D                  BNE   pr1   
E19D   20 B8 E1               JSR   tosget   
E1A0   C9 60                  CMP   #60h   
E1A2   90 04                  BCC   pr2   
E1A4   C9 7F                  CMP   #7Fh   
E1A6   90 E7                  BCC   pesc0   ; 60h-7Eh, and the carry is clear
E1A8   29 BF        PR2:      AND   #0BFh   
E1AA   20 03 FF     PR1:      JSR   CONOUT   
E1AD   4C 92 E1               JMP   pr0   
E1B0   A5 02        H_EMIT:   LDA   TL   ; "'"
E1B2   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E1B5   4C 0B E3     PDROP:    JMP   drop   
E1B8                             ; tosget: A = the byte at TOS, and TOS moves on.  inctos: TOS moves on.
E1B8   A0 00        TOSGET:   LDY   #0   
E1BA   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E1BC   E6 02        INCTOS:   INC   TL   
E1BE   D0 02                  BNE   tg1   
E1C0   E6 03                  INC   TH   
E1C2   60           TG1:      RTS      
E1C3                             ; pesc: the escapes of "$". A = the character after the "/", 60h to 7Eh, and
E1C3                             ; the carry is clear. Each returns into the loop.
E1C3                             ;    /a-/z   print the variable, as "#" does
E1C3                             ;    /{      clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
E1C3                             ;    /}      clear from the cursor to the end of the line
E1C3                             ;    /|  /`  show the cursor, hide it
E1C3                             ;    /~      ( row col addr -- addr ): the cursor to that row and column,
E1C3                             ;            from 0. The two cells under TOS (the string's address) go.
E1C3                             ; A - 7Bh sorts them: 00bbIDAsIHwgMSwg 2, ~ 3 with the carry set, and ` E5h, a-z
E1C3                             ; E6h-FFh with it clear.
E1C3                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's routines do the work.
                    PESC:     SBC   #7Ah   ; (the carry is clear: - 7Bh)
                              BCC   pe1   
                              BEQ   pcls   ; {
                              LSR      ; | 0, } 1, ~ 1; the carry set for | and ~
                              BEQ   pcur   ; |  show: the carry is set
                              BCS   pat   ; ~
                              JMP   CONEOL   ; }
                    PCLS:     JMP   CONCLS   
                    PE1:      CMP   #0E6h   
                              BCS   pvar   
                    PCUR:     JMP   CONCUR   ; `  hide: the carry is clear
E1C3                          ENDIF      
E1C3                             ; /~: the column is NOS, the row the cell under it.
E1C3                PAT:         
E1C3                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CPX   #DSE-2   ; fewer than two cells under TOS: s
                              BCS   e_atu   
E1C3                          ENDIF      
E1C3                          IF   1-ANSI   
                              LDY   DSL,X   ; the column
                              LDA   DSL+1,X   ; the row
                              INX      
                              INX      
                              JMP   CONAT   
E1C3                          ENDIF      
E1C3                          IF   ANSI   
E1C3                             ; ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H (ANSI counts from 1). The row's cell and TOS change
E1C3                             ; places first: then "#" prints the row and drops it, prints the column and
E1C3                             ; drops it, and TOS is the string's address again.
E1C3   E8                     INX      
E1C4   20 C1 E3               JSR   h_swap   
E1C7   CA                     DEX      
E1C8   A0 15                  LDY   #M_CSI-MSG   
E1CA   20 2E E2               JSR   prs   ; ESC [
E1CD   20 BC E1               JSR   inctos   
E1D0   20 EB E1               JSR   h_num   ; the row + 1
E1D3   A9 3B                  LDA   #";"   
E1D5   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E1D8   20 BC E1               JSR   inctos   
E1DB   20 EB E1               JSR   h_num   ; the column + 1
E1DE   A9 48                  LDA   #"H"   
E1E0   4C 03 FF               JMP   CONOUT   
E1E3                          ENDIF      
E1E3                          IF   CHECKED   
                    E_ATU:    JMP   e_stack   ; (X is FAh-FCh: an underflow)
E1E3                          ENDIF      
E1E3                             ; a-z: the carry is set. A + 3Ah is the letter - 41h, as step hands it to
E1E3                             ; lower: that pushes the variable"s address, "@" fetches it, and "#' (next)
E1E3                             ; prints it and drops it: TOS is the string's address again.
E1E3   69 39        PVAR:     ADC   #39h   
E1E5   20 F8 E0               JSR   lower   
E1E8   20 4F E4               JSR   h_fetch   
E1EB                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it. The
E1EB                             ; digits are divided off and held on the hardware stack, ended by a 0.
E1EB   A5 03        H_NUM:    LDA   TH   
E1ED   10 08                  BPL   pn1   
E1EF   A9 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
E1F1   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E1F4   20 67 E3               JSR   neg   
E1F7   A9 0A        PN1:      LDA   #10   
E1F9   85 08                  STA   D0   
E1FB   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E1FD   85 09                  STA   D1   
E1FF   48                     PHA      ; the end marker
E200   20 17 E4     PN2:      JSR   udiv   
E203   A5 04                  LDA   T0   ; the remainder
E205   09 30                  ORA   #"0"   
E207   48                     PHA      
E208   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E20A   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E20C   D0 F2                  BNE   pn2   
E20E   68           PN3:      PLA      
E20F   F0 A4                  BEQ   pdrop   
E211   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E214   4C 0E E2               JMP   pn3   
E217                          IF   ANSI   
E217                             ; With ANSI = 1 they are sequences, each a message at MSG, printed by prs,
E217                             ; which pesc runs on into. (It sits here, just above prs, for that.)
E217   E9 7A        PESC:     SBC   #7Ah   ; (the carry is clear: - 7Bh). Y is 0, as
E219                             ;   tosget leaves it, and M_CLS is the first
E219                             ;   message: Y already points at it
E219   90 0D                  BCC   pe1   
E21B   F0 11                  BEQ   prs   ; {  ESC [ H ESC [ J
E21D   A0 06                  LDY   #M_SHOW-MSG   
E21F   4A                     LSR      ; | 0, } 1, ~ 1; the carry set for ~
E220   F0 0C                  BEQ   prs   ; |  ESC [ ? 2 5 h
E222   B0 9F                  BCS   pat   ; ~
E224   A0 12                  LDY   #M_EOL-MSG   ; }  ESC [ K
E226   D0 06                  BNE   prs   ; always
E228   C9 E6        PE1:      CMP   #0E6h   
E22A   B0 B7                  BCS   pvar   
E22C   A0 0C                  LDY   #M_HIDE-MSG   ; `  ESC [ ? 2 5 l, and on into prs
E22E                          ENDIF      
E22E                          IF   CHECKED+ANSI   
E22E                             ; prs: print the message at MSG+Y; its last byte has bit 7 set. Y ends just
E22E                             ; past it, at the next message.
E22E   B9 3C E2     PRS:      LDA   MSG,Y   
E231   48                     PHA      
E232   29 7F                  AND   #7Fh   
E234   20 03 FF               JSR   CONOUT   
E237   C8                     INY      
E238   68                     PLA      
E239   10 F3                  BPL   prs   
E23B   60                     RTS      
E23C                MSG:         
E23C                          ENDIF      
E23C                          IF   ANSI   
E23C   1B 5B 48 1B 5B CA M_CLS:   DB   27,"[","H",27,"[","J"+80h   ; (the first: pesc counts on it)
E242   1B 5B 3F 32 35 E8 M_SHOW:   DB   27,"[","?","2","5","h"+80h   
E248   1B 5B 3F 32 35 EC M_HIDE:   DB   27,"[","?","2","5","l"+80h   
E24E   1B 5B CB     M_EOL:    DB   27,"[","K"+80h   
E251   1B DB        M_CSI:    DB   27,"["+80h   
E253                          ENDIF      
E253                          IF   CHECKED   
                    M_ERR:    DB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
                              DB   " @"," "+80h   
                    M_NL:     DB   13,10+80h   
                    M_STK:    DB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
                    M_CD:     DB   ": ..","."+80h   
                    M_C:      DB   ":"+80h   
                    M_RTN:    DB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
E253                          ENDIF      
E253                             ; =============================================================================
E253                             ;  Dispatch table: one handler per punctuation character, in code order.
E253                             ;  Entries are handler-1 for the RTS trick.
E253                             ; =============================================================================
E253   FB E2        PTAB:     DW   h_store-1   ; !
E255   7A E1                  DW   h_str-1   ; "
E257   EA E1                  DW   h_num-1   ; #
E259   91 E1                  DW   h_print-1   ; $
E25B   C0 E3                  DW   h_swap-1   ; %
E25D   16 E3                  DW   h_and-1   ; &
E25F   AF E1                  DW   h_emit-1   ; '
E261   16 E1                  DW   h_open-1   ; (
E263   4D E0                  DW   h_close-1   ; )
E265   99 E3                  DW   h_mul-1   ; *
E267   48 E3                  DW   h_add-1   ; +
E269   5A E4                  DW   h_cfetch-1   ; ,
E26B   40 E3                  DW   h_sub-1   ; -
E26D   02 E3                  DW   h_cstore-1   ; .
E26F   D5 E3                  DW   h_div-1   ; /
E271   0A E1                  DW   push-1   ; :
E273   0A E3                  DW   drop-1   ; ;
E275   77 E3                  DW   h_lt-1   ; <
E277   89 E3                  DW   h_eq-1   ; =
E279   74 E3                  DW   h_gt-1   ; >
E27B   63 E4                  DW   h_key-1   ; ?
E27D   4E E4                  DW   h_fetch-1   ; @
E27F   32 E1                  DW   h_def-1   ; [
E281   64 E0                  DW   h_break-1   ; \
E283   53 E0                  DW   h_ret-1   ; ]
E285   32 E3                  DW   h_xor-1   ; ^
E287   FF E3                  DW   h_alloc-1   ; _
E289   C1 E4                  DW   h_grave-1   ; `
E28B   33 E0                  DW   h_tor-1   ; {
E28D   24 E3                  DW   h_or-1   ; |
E28F   40 E0                  DW   h_fromr-1   ; }
E291   60 E3                  DW   h_not-1   ; ~
E293                             ; rdnum: TOS = TOS*10 + digit for each digit at IP. Wraps at 16 bits. The
E293                             ; test is at the bottom so the loop closes with a branch. Returns with the
E293                             ; carry set.
E293   20 E1 E2     RD1:      JSR   incip   ; (keeps A = the digit)
E296   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E298   26 03                  ROL   TH   ; x2
E29A   18                     CLC      
E29B   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E29D   85 04                  STA   T0   
E29F   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E2A1   69 00                  ADC   #0   
E2A3   A8                     TAY      ; Y:T0 = x2 + digit
E2A4   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E2A6   26 03                  ROL   TH   
E2A8   06 02                  ASL   TL   
E2AA   26 03                  ROL   TH   ; x8
E2AC   18                     CLC      
E2AD   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E2AF   65 04                  ADC   T0   
E2B1   85 02                  STA   TL   
E2B3   98                     TYA      
E2B4   65 03                  ADC   TH   
E2B6   85 03                  STA   TH   ; x8 + x2 + digit
E2B8   20 BE E2     RDNUM:    JSR   isdig   
E2BB   90 D6                  BCC   rd1   
E2BD   60                     RTS      
E2BE                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is clear if it is a
E2BE                             ; digit. Y = 0.
E2BE   20 D9 E2     ISDIG:    JSR   peek   
E2C1   38                     SEC      
E2C2   E9 30                  SBC   #"0"   
E2C4   C9 0A                  CMP   #10   
E2C6   60                     RTS      
E2C7                             ; =============================================================================
E2C7                             ;  Reading the program
E2C7                             ;    peek: A = the character at IP, IP unchanged, Y = 0
E2C7                             ;    getc: the same, then IP moves on; flags follow A
E2C7                             ;    incip: IP moves on; keeps A, the carry and Y
E2C7                             ; =============================================================================
E2C7                             ; rdhex: if IP is at a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), return its value in A with
E2C7                             ; the carry clear and IP moved on; otherwise the carry is set and IP stays.
E2C7                             ; Y = 0.
E2C7   20 BE E2     RDHEX:    JSR   isdig   
E2CA   90 0A                  BCC   rh1   
E2CC   29 DF                  AND   #0DFh   
E2CE   E9 11                  SBC   #11h   ; (the carry is set)
E2D0   C9 06                  CMP   #6   
E2D2   B0 04                  BCS   rh9   
E2D4   69 0A                  ADC   #10   
E2D6   90 09        RH1:      BCC   incip   ; always: the carry is clear
E2D8   60           RH9:      RTS      
E2D9   A0 00        PEEK:     LDY   #0   
E2DB   B1 00                  LDA   (IP),Y   
E2DD   60                     RTS      
E2DE   20 D9 E2     GETC:     JSR   peek   
E2E1   E6 00        INCIP:    INC   IP   
E2E3   D0 02                  BNE   ic1   
E2E5   E6 01                  INC   IP+1   
E2E7   09 00        IC1:      ORA   #0   
E2E9   60                     RTS      
E2EA                             ; rstip: point IP at the start of the program
E2EA   A9 00        RSTIP:    LDA   #<PROG   
E2EC   85 00                  STA   IP   
E2EE   A9 05                  LDA   #>PROG   
E2F0   85 01                  STA   IP+1   
E2F2   60                     RTS      
E2F3                             ; =============================================================================
E2F3                             ;  Stack
E2F3                             ; =============================================================================
E2F3                             ; flag: pops TOS and returns with Z set if it was 0. Keeps the carry.
E2F3   A5 02        FLAG:     LDA   TL   
E2F5   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E2F7   20 0B E3               JSR   drop   
E2FA   A8                     TAY      ; (drop's INX changed the flags)
E2FB   60                     RTS      
E2FC                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." plus the high byte. Both end in drop.
E2FC                H_STORE:      
E2FC                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDA   TL   ; both bytes must be in the program's space:
                              ADC   #1   ; check the page of addr+1 (the carry is
                              LDA   TH   ; clear on the way in)
                              ADC   #0   
                              JSR   chkst   
E2FC                          ENDIF      
E2FC   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E2FF   A0 01                  LDY   #1   
E301   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E303                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
E303                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDA   TH   
                              JSR   chkst   
E303                          ENDIF      
E303   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E306   A0 00                  LDY   #0   
E308   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E30A   E8                     INX      ; falls into drop
E30B                             ; drop: ";" and every drop. It works through Y, so A and the carry are kept;
E30B                             ; it returns with Z clear.
E30B   BC 00 02     DROP:     LDY   DSL,X   
E30E   84 02                  STY   TL   
E310   BC 00 03               LDY   DSH,X   
E313   84 03                  STY   TH   
E315   E8                     INX      
E316   60                     RTS      
E317                             ; =============================================================================
E317                             ;  Arithmetic and logic. Effects are ( NOS TOS -- result ).
E317                             ; =============================================================================
E317                             ; The logic operators leave the carry as they found it, clear, so they can
E317                             ; branch to fin.
E317   BD 00 02     H_AND:    LDA   DSL,X   
E31A   25 02                  AND   TL   
E31C   85 02                  STA   TL   
E31E   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E321   25 03                  AND   TH   
E323   90 31                  BCC   fin   ; always
E325   BD 00 02     H_OR:     LDA   DSL,X   
E328   05 02                  ORA   TL   
E32A   85 02                  STA   TL   
E32C   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E32F   05 03                  ORA   TH   
E331   90 23                  BCC   fin   ; always
E333   BD 00 02     H_XOR:    LDA   DSL,X   
E336   45 02                  EOR   TL   
E338   85 02                  STA   TL   
E33A   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E33D   45 03                  EOR   TH   
E33F   90 15                  BCC   fin   ; always
E341                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
E341   20 BE E2     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
E344   90 14                  BCC   negnum   
E346   20 67 E3     SUB1:     JSR   neg   ; a - b = a + (-b)
E349   18           H_ADD:    CLC      
E34A   BD 00 02               LDA   DSL,X   
E34D   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E34F   85 02                  STA   TL   
E351   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E354   65 03                  ADC   TH   ; falls into fin
E356                             ; fin: finish a two-operand op: A = the high byte of the result
E356   85 03        FIN:      STA   TH   
E358   E8                     INX      
E359   60                     RTS      
E35A   A9 00        NEGNUM:   LDA   #0   ; a number from 0 (the digit routine's start)
E35C   20 F0 E0               JSR   digit   ; (comes back with the carry set)
E35F   B0 06                  BCS   neg   ; always: the number, negated
E361                             ; "~": -x - 1, which is neg with the carry clear, as it is here
E361   90 05        H_NOT:    BCC   neg1   ; always
E363                             ; absv: TOS = |TOS|.  negm: TOS = -TOS if the N flag is set.
E363   A5 03        ABSV:     LDA   TH   
E365   10 0D        NEGM:     BPL   ab9   
E367                             ; neg: TOS = -TOS
E367   38           NEG:      SEC      
E368   A9 00        NEG1:     LDA   #0   
E36A   E5 02                  SBC   TL   
E36C   85 02                  STA   TL   
E36E   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E370   E5 03                  SBC   TH   
E372   85 03                  STA   TH   
E374   60           AB9:      RTS      
E375                             ; Signed compares: a - b sets N and V; N xor V is "a < b". The carry ends up
E375                             ; clear for true, and bool turns it into -1 (true) or 0 (both pop NOS first).
E375   20 C1 E3     H_GT:     JSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
E378   BD 00 02     H_LT:     LDA   DSL,X   
E37B   C5 02                  CMP   TL   
E37D   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E380   E5 03                  SBC   TH   
E382   70 02                  BVS   lt1   
E384   49 80                  EOR   #80h   
E386   0A           LT1:      ASL      
E387   E8                     INX      ; (keeps the carry; never leaves X at 0)
E388   D0 07                  BNE   bool   ; always
E38A   20 46 E3     H_EQ:     JSR   sub1   ; a - b: zero if equal; A = its high byte
E38D   05 02                  ORA   TL   
E38F   C9 01                  CMP   #1   ; carry clear if A = 0
E391   A9 00        BOOL:     LDA   #0   
E393   69 FF                  ADC   #0FFh   ; carry clear: FF, set: 00
E395   85 02                  STA   TL   
E397   85 03                  STA   TH   
E399   60                     RTS      
E39A                             ; "*": the classic shift-right multiply. The multiplier leaves TH:TL from the
E39A                             ; bottom while the product comes in at the top, through A:T0 above it; after
E39A                             ; 16 rounds TH:TL hold the low 16 bits, which are all that is kept.
E39A   A0 10        H_MUL:    LDY   #16   ; the round count
E39C   A9 00                  LDA   #0   
E39E   85 04                  STA   T0   ; A:T0 = the upper half
E3A0   46 03                  LSR   TH   
E3A2   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; the first multiplier bit
E3A4   90 0F        ML1:      BCC   ml2   
E3A6   85 05                  STA   T1   
E3A8   18                     CLC      
E3A9   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E3AB   7D 00 02               ADC   DSL,X   
E3AE   85 04                  STA   T0   
E3B0   A5 05                  LDA   T1   
E3B2   7D 00 03               ADC   DSH,X   ; upper half += the multiplicand
E3B5   6A           ML2:      ROR      
E3B6   66 04                  ROR   T0   
E3B8   66 03                  ROR   TH   
E3BA   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; everything one place right; next bit out
E3BC   88                     DEY      
E3BD   D0 E5                  BNE   ml1   
E3BF   E8                     INX      ; drop the multiplicand
E3C0   60                     RTS      
E3C1   BC 00 02     H_SWAP:   LDY   DSL,X   ; "%"
E3C4   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E3C6   9D 00 02               STA   DSL,X   
E3C9   84 02                  STY   TL   
E3CB   BC 00 03               LDY   DSH,X   
E3CE   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E3D0   9D 00 03               STA   DSH,X   
E3D3   84 03                  STY   TH   
E3D5   60                     RTS      
E3D6                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
E3D6                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b, r is pushed
E3D6                             ; and gets the sign of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no
E3D6                             ; meaning; checked, it stops with Z.
E3D6                H_DIV:       
E3D6                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LDA   TL   
                              ORA   TH   
                              BEQ   e_zero   
E3D6                          ENDIF      
E3D6   BD 00 03               LDA   DSH,X   
E3D9   48                     PHA      ; a's sign: for r
E3DA   45 03                  EOR   TH   
E3DC   48                     PHA      ; a xor b: for q
E3DD   20 63 E3               JSR   absv   
E3E0   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E3E2   85 08                  STA   D0   
E3E4   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E3E6   85 09                  STA   D1   ; D = |b|
E3E8   20 0B E3               JSR   drop   ; TOS = a
E3EB   20 63 E3               JSR   absv   ; TOS = |a|
E3EE   20 17 E4               JSR   udiv   ; TOS = q, T0/T1 = r
E3F1   68                     PLA      
E3F2   20 65 E3               JSR   negm   ; q's sign
E3F5   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E3F7   A4 05                  LDY   T1   
E3F9   20 01 E1               JSR   pushay   ; r on top
E3FC   68                     PLA      
E3FD   4C 65 E3               JMP   negm   ; r's sign
E400                             ; =============================================================================
E400                             ;  Storage
E400                             ; =============================================================================
E400                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap top moves by n, which is signed: a negative
E400                             ; count releases. TOS becomes the old top. (The carry is clear on the way in.)
E400                          IF   1-CHECKED   
E400   AD 7C 04     H_ALLOC:   LDA   HEAP   
E403   A8                     TAY      
E404   65 02                  ADC   TL   
E406   8D 7C 04               STA   HEAP   
E409   84 02                  STY   TL   
E40B   AD 7D 04               LDA   HEAP+1   
E40E   A8                     TAY      
E40F   65 03                  ADC   TH   
E411   8D 7D 04               STA   HEAP+1   
E414   84 03                  STY   TH   
E416   60                     RTS      
E417                          ENDIF      
E417                             ; The checked build works the new top out first, in T0 and Y, and stops with
E417                             ; H, the count still on the stack, if it is at or past the limit, below the
E417                             ; program's end, or if the 16-bit add wrapped. A wrap is the V flag of the
E417                             ; high bytes" add with the old top"s sign bit flipped: that makes the old top
E417                             ; a signed number from -8000h, so the add overflows exactly when the true
E417                             ; sum leaves 0000h-FFFFh.
E417                          IF   CHECKED   
                    H_ALLOC:   LDA   HEAP   
                              ADC   TL   
                              STA   T0   
                              LDA   HEAP+1   
                              EOR   #80h   
                              ADC   TH   
                              BVS   e_heap   ; wrapped
                              EOR   #80h   ; the new top's high byte
                              CMP   #HEAPLIM   
                              BCS   e_heap   ; at or past the limit
                              TAY      
                              LDA   T0   
                              CMP   PEND   
                              TYA      
                              SBC   PEND+1   
                              BCC   e_heap   ; below the program's end
                              LDA   HEAP   
                              STA   TL   
                              LDA   T0   
                              STA   HEAP   
                              LDA   HEAP+1   
                              STA   TH   
                              STY   HEAP+1   
                              RTS      
                                 ; Errors found by handlers. The stacks are as they were before the handler.
                    E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; divide by zero
                              DB   2Ch   ; (BIT abs: hides the next instruction)
                    E_HEAP:   LDA   #"H"   ; heap past the limit or below the program
                              DB   2Ch   
                    E_STORE:   LDA   #"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
                              JMP   error   
                                 ; chkst: stop unless the page in A is in the program's own space, from the
                                 ; letter page up to the heap limit. Keeps Y.
                    CHKST:    CMP   #LETPAGE   
                              BCC   e_store   
                              CMP   #HEAPLIM   
                              BCS   e_store   
                              RTS      
E417                          ENDIF      
E417                             ; udiv: unsigned TOS / D (D <= 8000h). TOS becomes the quotient and T0/T1
E417                             ; the remainder. The low byte of each trial subtraction waits on the
E417                             ; hardware stack.
E417                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
E417   A9 00        UDIV:     LDA   #0   
E419   85 04                  STA   T0   
E41B   85 05                  STA   T1   
E41D   A5 08                  LDA   D0   
E41F   49 02                  EOR   #2   
E421   05 09                  ORA   D1   
E423   D0 07                  BNE   ud0   
E425   46 03                  LSR   TH   
E427   66 02                  ROR   TL   ; the quotient
E429   26 04                  ROL   T0   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
E42B   60                     RTS      
E42C   A0 10        UD0:      LDY   #16   
E42E   06 02        UD1:      ASL   TL   
E430   26 03                  ROL   TH   
E432   26 04                  ROL   T0   
E434   26 05                  ROL   T1   
E436   38                     SEC      
E437   A5 04                  LDA   T0   
E439   E5 08                  SBC   D0   
E43B   48                     PHA      
E43C   A5 05                  LDA   T1   
E43E   E5 09                  SBC   D1   
E440   90 08                  BCC   ud2   
E442   85 05                  STA   T1   
E444   68                     PLA      
E445   85 04                  STA   T0   
E447   E6 02                  INC   TL   ; the quotient bit (TL's bit 0 is free)
E449   24                     DB   24h   ; (BIT zp: steps over the PLA)
E44A   68           UD2:      PLA      
E44B   88                     DEY      
E44C   D0 E0                  BNE   ud1   
E44E   60                     RTS      
E44F                             ; =============================================================================
E44F                             ;  Console
E44F                             ; =============================================================================
E44F   A0 01        H_FETCH:   LDY   #1   ; "@"
E451   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E453   48                     PHA      ; the high byte, while "," gets the low one
E454   20 5B E4               JSR   h_cfetch   
E457   68                     PLA      
E458   85 03                  STA   TH   
E45A   60                     RTS      
E45B                H_CFETCH:      ; ","
E45B   A0 00                  LDY   #0   
E45D   B1 02                  LDA   (TL),Y   
E45F   85 02        CF2:      STA   TL   ; TOS = A (low), Y (high)
E461   84 03                  STY   TH   
E463   60                     RTS      
E464                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
E464                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
E464                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
E464                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
E464                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
E464   A5 03        H_KEY:    LDA   TH   
E466   30 20                  BMI   line   
E468   A0 28        KT1:      LDY   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
E46A   20 77 E0     KT2:      JSR   getk   
E46D   D0 15                  BNE   kt3   
E46F   88                     DEY      
E470   D0 F8                  BNE   kt2   
E472   A5 02                  LDA   TL   ; count the millisecond off:
E474   D0 06                  BNE   kt4   
E476   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E478   F0 EE                  BEQ   kt1   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
E47A   C6 03                  DEC   TH   
E47C   C6 02        KT4:      DEC   TL   
E47E   D0 E8                  BNE   kt1   
E480   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E482   D0 E4                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
E484   A0 00        KT3:      LDY   #0   
E486   F0 D7                  BEQ   cf2   ; always: TOS = A
E488                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
E488                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
E488                             ; is full. Y = the length so far; TL = the most allowed.
E488   20 67 E3     LINE:     JSR   neg   ; TOS = the count, and A = its high byte
E48B   D0 04                  BNE   ln0   
E48D   A5 02                  LDA   TL   
E48F   10 04                  BPL   ln1   
E491   A9 7F        LN0:      LDA   #127   ; more than 127 is taken as 127
E493   85 02                  STA   TL   
E495   A0 00        LN1:      LDY   #0   
E497   F0 03                  BEQ   ln2   ; always
E499   20 03 FF     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
E49C   20 77 E0     LN2:      JSR   getk   
E49F   F0 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
E4A1   C9 0D                  CMP   #13   
E4A3   F0 14                  BEQ   ln5   
E4A5   C9 08                  CMP   #8   
E4A7   F0 0A                  BEQ   ln4   
E4A9   C4 02                  CPY   TL   
E4AB   B0 EF                  BCS   ln2   ; full
E4AD   99 80 04               STA   LINEBUF,Y   
E4B0   C8                     INY      
E4B1   D0 E6                  BNE   ln3   ; always: echo it
E4B3   88           LN4:      DEY      ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
E4B4   10 E3                  BPL   ln3   
E4B6   C8                     INY      ;   unless the line was empty
E4B7   F0 E3                  BEQ   ln2   ; always
E4B9   99 80 04     LN5:      STA   LINEBUF,Y   ; A = CR
E4BC   A9 80                  LDA   #<LINEBUF   
E4BE   A0 04                  LDY   #>LINEBUF   
E4C0   D0 9D                  BNE   cf2   ; always: TOS = the line's address
E4C2                             ; =============================================================================
E4C2                             ;  Machine code: the grave
E4C2                             ; =============================================================================
E4C2                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
E4C2                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (60h) is
E4C2                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
E4C2                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ); see the
E4C2                             ; contract in the header.
E4C2   20 C7 E2     H_GRAVE:   JSR   rdhex   
E4C5   B0 1C                  BCS   exec   
E4C7   0A           HX1:      ASL      
E4C8   0A                     ASL      
E4C9   0A                     ASL      
E4CA   0A                     ASL      
E4CB   85 04                  STA   T0   
E4CD   20 C7 E2               JSR   rdhex   
E4D0   B0 0C                  BCS   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
E4D2   05 04                  ORA   T0   
E4D4   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   ; Y is 0 after rdhex (never checked)
E4D6   20 BC E1               JSR   inctos   
E4D9   20 C7 E2               JSR   rdhex   
E4DC   90 E9                  BCC   hx1   
E4DE   A9 60        HX2:      LDA   #60h   
E4E0   91 02                  STA   (TL),Y   
E4E2   60                     RTS      
E4E3   A5 02        EXEC:     LDA   TL   
E4E5   85 04                  STA   T0   
E4E7   A5 03                  LDA   TH   
E4E9   85 05                  STA   T1   
E4EB   20 0B E3               JSR   drop   ; the address is consumed
E4EE   6C 04 00               JMP   (T0)   
E4F1                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; =============================================================================
                                 ;  Checked build: the error report
                                 ; =============================================================================
                                 ; error: the report, then EXIT. A = the letter, PLACE = the place, X = the
                                 ; data stack to show, RSV = S for the Rtn line. Nothing here relies on S: an
                                 ; overflowed or underflowed hardware stack wraps inside its page, and only
                                 ; its depth is shown.
                                 ;   CR LF
                                 ;   Err X @ line,col CR LF
                                 ;   up to 16 characters from the place, raw, up to a CR, LF or NUL  CR LF
                                 ;   Stk n: [...] and the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top  CR LF
                                 ;   Rtn n CR LF
                                 ; The numbers go through "#" (prnum), which pushes them over the data stack
                                 ; and pops them again, so the stack is shown as it was.
                    ERROR:    PHA      ; the letter
                              LDY   #M_ERR-MSG   
                              JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Err "
                              PLA      
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              JSR   prs   ; " @ " (it follows M_ERR)
                              JSR   lcol   
                              LDA   D0   
                              LDY   D1   
                              JSR   prnum   ; the line
                              LDA   #","   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              LDA   CL   
                              LDY   CL+1   
                              JSR   prnum   ; the column
                              LDY   #M_NL-MSG   
                              JSR   prs   
                              LDY   #0   ; the text at the place
                    ER1:      LDA   (PLACE),Y   
                              BEQ   er2   
                              CMP   #13   
                              BEQ   er2   
                              CMP   #10   
                              BEQ   er2   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              INY      
                              CPY   #16   
                              BNE   er1   
                    ER2:      LDY   #M_STK-MSG   
                              JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Stk "
                              TXA      
                              EOR   #0FFh   
                              SEC      
                              SBC   #0FFh-DSE   ; the depth, DSE - X (FFh, an overflow: 253)
                              PHA      
                              JSR   prnum8   
                              PLA      
                              LDY   #M_C-MSG   ; ":"
                              CMP   #9   
                              BCC   er3   
                              LDA   #8   ; more than 8: ": ..." and the top 8
                              LDY   #M_CD-MSG   
                    ER3:      STA   T2   ; T2 = how many cells to show (the place
                                 ;   is no longer needed)
                              JSR   prs   
                              JSR   push   ; TOS into memory with the rest: cell i from
                                 ;   the top is at DSL+X+i now
                    ER4:      LDA   T2   ; cells T2-1 down to 0, the top last
                              BEQ   er5   
                              DEC   T2   
                              LDA   #" "   
                              JSR   CONOUT   
                              TXA      
                              CLC      
                              ADC   T2   
                              TAY      
                              LDA   DSL,Y   
                              PHA      
                              LDA   DSH,Y   
                              TAY      
                              PLA      
                              JSR   prnum   
                              JMP   er4   
                    ER5:      LDY   #M_RTN-MSG   
                              JSR   prs   ; CR LF "Rtn "
                              LDA   RSV   
                              EOR   #0FFh   
                              LSR      ; (FFh - S) / 2 entries
                              JSR   prnum8   
                              LDY   #M_NL-MSG   
                              JSR   prs   
                              JMP   EXIT   
                                 ; prnum: print the number A (low), Y (high), signed, keeping the data stack.
                                 ; prnum8: the same for A alone, 0-255.
                    PRNUM8:   LDY   #0   
                    PRNUM:    JSR   pushay   
                              JMP   h_num   
                                 ; lcol: the line (D0/D1) and the column (CL) of the place, both from 1. A
                                 ; place below the program is in the -n? line buffer: line 0, and the column
                                 ; is the place in the buffer. Otherwise IP (free now: the program has
                                 ; stopped) runs from PROG to the place, counting LFs; CL keeps where the
                                 ; last line started, and the column is the place minus that, plus 1.
                    LCOL:     LDA   #0   
                              STA   D1   
                              STA   D0   
                              LDA   #<LINEBUF   
                              STA   CL   
                              LDA   #>LINEBUF   
                              STA   CL+1   
                              LDA   PLACE   
                              CMP   #<PROG   
                              LDA   PLACE+1   
                              SBC   #>PROG   
                              BCC   lc9   ; below the program: line 0
                              INC   D0   
                              JSR   rstip   
                    LC3:      LDA   IP   ; a line starts here
                              STA   CL   
                              LDA   IP+1   
                              STA   CL+1   
                    LC1:      LDA   IP   
                              CMP   PLACE   
                              LDA   IP+1   
                              SBC   PLACE+1   
                              BCS   lc9   ; at the place
                              JSR   getc   
                              CMP   #10   
                              BNE   lc1   
                              INC   D0   ; an LF: a new line starts after it
                              BNE   lc3   
                              INC   D1   
                              BNE   lc3   ; always
                    LC9:      LDA   PLACE   
                              SEC      
                              SBC   CL   
                              STA   CL   
